// The version of the mod API. It only grows: each version adds to `Game` and
// `Mod` and removes nothing, so a game runs mods built for its version or an
// earlier one, and refuses newer ones. The harness reads this same constant.
//   1: Game's ships, conditions and messages; on_load and on_step.
//   2: the galaxy, world changes, governments, spawning, map overlays, the
//      planet button and panels; on_day, on_enter, on_planet_button, on_panel.
//   3: Game.fleet_stat (a fleet's hull, shields, dps, speed, ships and cost),
//      system_fleet_count and system_fleet.
//   4: Game.map_detail, a section of the map's side panel for a system.
//   5: the outfitter button (Game.outfitter_button; can_outfitter, on_outfitter),
//      the player's fleet by UUID, outfits and integrating them
//      (Game.ship_integrate), and Game.confirm with on_confirm.
//   6: per-pilot mod storage (Game.data, set_data), planets (planet,
//      planet_at, planet_service, ...), tables in the panel (panel_columns,
//      panel_row; on_panel_row), and Game.ask_number with on_number.
//   7: a full screen for the panel (Game.screen_open), a chosen row
//      (panel_select), and clicks on its column headings (on_panel_header).
//   8: charts on the screen's sidebar (Game.panel_chart), and jobs on the job
//      board (Game.offer_job).
//   9: shipyard stock (Game.ship_stock_on, ship_stock, set_ship_stock,
//      ship_order_note, ship_in_stock), shipyard listings and ship models
//      (shipyard_count, shipyard_model, model_name, model_cost,
//      model_category, model_licenses), buy_ship, the ships destroyed each
//      step (losses, loss_model, loss_government, loss_by_player), and
//      map_label and map_ring.
package es

const i64 MOD_API = 9
